[5990]="70022746\n1\tDestroy tribute-piles (total: 3)\tTribute-piles can be found outside Gunnberg's lair, south of Zudrugund. Frithgeir has asked you to seek out Gunnberg's tribute-piles and destroy them.\n2\tGunnberg's personal tribute-pile lies outside his home in a small mountain pass. Frithgeir has asked you to disturb Gunnberg's personal tribute-pile and draw him forth to battle.\t\n3\tTalk to Frithgeir at Zudrugund\tFrithgeir is at Zudrugund, north of the giant-ruins. You should return to Frithgeir with news of Gunnberg's defeat.\n",
[5991]="7003E2F4\n1\tDefeat Gurthagar\tGurthagar can be found in the eastern Fields of Fornost, near Amon Amrûn. You should defeat Gurthagar, for this being has sapped the life from the Fields of Fornost.\n2\tDefeat Gurthagar\tGurthagar can be found in the eastern Fields of Fornost, near Amon Amrûn. You should defeat Gurthagar, for this being has sapped the life from the Fields of Fornost.\n3\tCompleted\tYou have defeated one of the chief forces of evil in the Fields of Fornost.\n",
[5992]="70068BE3\n1\tClean up the detritus (total: 6)\tAhûzath has asked you to clean up all the detritus in the Gut.\n2\tTalk to Ahûzath\tYou have cleaned up most of the mess in the Gut. You should tell Ahûzath about this.\n",
[5993]="70027E82\n1\tFind Guto at his encampment\tGuto has made camp south-east of the watch-tower in Trum Dreng. You should seek out Guto and help him track the Dragon-clan chieftain who has stirred up so much trouble.\n",
[5994]="7006432F\n1\tDefeat Gurkrak\tGurkrak keeps watch on Gwathrenost and brutally dispatches those foolish or daring enough to enter the Witch-king's citadel unbidden.\n2\tDefeat Castellan Obáshurz\tOne of the last remnants of the reign of the Steward of Angmar, Castellan Obáshurz tends Gwathrenost and dutifully serves his masters: High Priestess Ásachal and High Chieftain Claghórd.\n3\tDefeat High Priestess Ásachal and High Chieftain Claghórd\tHigh Priestess Ásachal and High Chieftain Claghórd await in Tham Mornarcham, the Seat of the the Witch-king. High Priestess Ásachal and High Chieftain Claghórd must be defeated before they can wield the Shard of Tauressar to subjugate the Free Peoples of Middle-earth.\n4\tDestroy the Shard of Tauressar\tSevered from the Vandassar of Rhudaur, the Shard of Tauressar is possessed of a terrible enchantment capable of swaying the hearts and minds of those who swear oaths upon it—willingly or not. You must destroy the Shard of Tauressar.\n",
