[5998]="70064333\n1\tDefeat Gurkrak\tGurkrak keeps watch on Gwathrenost and brutally dispatches those foolish or daring enough to enter the Witch-king's citadel unbidden.\n2\tDefeat Castellan Obáshurz\tOne of the last remnants of the reign of the Steward of Angmar, Castellan Obáshurz tends Gwathrenost and dutifully serves his masters: High Priestess Ásachal and High Chieftain Claghórd.\n3\tDefeat High Priestess Ásachal and High Chieftain Claghórd\tHigh Priestess Ásachal and High Chieftain Claghórd await in Tham Mornarcham, the Seat of the the Witch-king. High Priestess Ásachal and High Chieftain Claghórd must be defeated before they can wield the Shard of Tauressar to subjugate the Free Peoples of Middle-earth.\n4\tDestroy the Shard of Tauressar\tSevered from the Vandassar of Rhudaur, the Shard of Tauressar is possessed of a terrible enchantment capable of swaying the hearts and minds of those who swear oaths upon it—willingly or not. You must destroy the Shard of Tauressar.\n",
[5999]="70064EDE\n1\tTalk to Chiver Me Timbers\tBy completing this quest, you will automatically complete the Gwathrenost, the Witch-king's Citadel, tiers 2 through 4 instance deeds.\n",
[6000]="7006463B\n1\tImprisoned Hill-men can be found at Gwathrenost. Raith has asked you to free Hill-men that have been imprisoned by the Iron Crown from Gwathrenost.\t\n2\tTalk to Raith at Bail Avarc\tRaith can be found at Bail Avarc. You have freed many of the Hill-men imprisoned by the Iron Crown from Gwathrenost. You should return to Raith.\n",
[6001]="7006461F\n1\tCollect scrolls of forgotten history in Gwathrenost (total: 6)\tIron Crown repositories containing scrolls of forgotten history can be found at Gwathrenost. Raith has asked you to search the Iron Crown's repositories at Gwathrenost for scrolls of forgotten history, as the oppression of the Witch-king of Angmar and the Iron Crown has done much to obscure the true history of Angmar.\n2\tDeliver the scrolls of forgotten history to Raith at Bail Avarc\tRaith can be found at Bail Avarc. You have collected several scrolls of forgotten history from the repositories at Gwathrenost. You should deliver them to Raith.\n",
[6002]="7006463C\n1\tDestroy banners of the Iron Crown (total: 12)\tBanners of the Iron Crown can be found at Gwathrenost. Raith has asked you to destroy banners of the Iron Crown at Gwathrenost.\n2\tTalk to Raith at Bail Avarc\tRaith can be found at Bail Avarc. You have destroyed many of the Iron Crown's banners at Gwathrenost. You should return to Raith.\n",
[6003]="70059839\n1\tDefeat Gwengorn the white stag\tThe white stag can be found in the south-western Wildwood. Linnet has asked you to defeat Gwengorn the white stag.\n2\tPursue the white stag\tGwengorn has fled into the hills of the southern Wildwood. You should pursue Gwengorn.\n3\tExamine the net trap\tGwengorn has led you to a sprung trap in the southern Wildwood. You should examine the trap.\n4\tTalk to Linnet\tLinnet is located in the south-central Wildwood. You should talk to Linnet Redholm.\n",
[6004]="70007F08\n1\tBring the cave-claw legs to Ormr\030Collect cave-claw legs (total: 8)\tCave-claws can be found in the old mine east of Thorin's Hall. Ormr is on the road south from Thorin's Hall to Noglond. Ormr has asked you to collect the last ingredient he needs to prepare Gísli's favourite meal: cave-claw legs.\n2\tBring Gísli the meal prepared by his father\tGísli is at Noglond, south of Thorin's Halls. Ormr finished preparing the stew for his son and asked you to deliver it to Gísli for him.\n",
[6005]="7005342F\n1\tTalk to the Protectors of the Vales to trade Gúlmarks for Motes. This quest can be completed weekly. Completing this quest will remove 55 Gúlmarks.\t\n",
[6006]="7005AB4A\n1\tDeliver the ancient sword sheaths to a collection box\030Collect ancient sword sheaths (total: 10)\tYou have accepted a task to acquire ancient sword sheaths for the Haban'akkâ of Thráin.\n",
[6007]="7005AB49\n1\tDeliver the cracked lances to a collection box\030Collect cracked lances (total: 10)\tYou have accepted a task to acquire cracked lances for the Haban'akkâ of Thráin.\n",
[6008]="7005AB4C\n1\tDeliver the night-touched furs to a collection box\030Collect night-touched furs (total: 10)\tYou have accepted a task to acquire night-touched furs for the Haban'akkâ of Thráin.\n",
[6009]="7005AB4B\n1\tDeliver the sinister wings to a collection box\030Collect sinister wings (total: 10)\tYou have accepted a task to acquire sinister wings for the Haban'akkâ of Thráin.\n",
[6010]="700571B0\n1\tLearn the history of the Rohirrim with Léothred\tFramsburg can be found in Misthallow. You should learn the history of the Rohirrim with Léothred.\n2\tContinue learning the history of the Rohirrim with Léothred\tFramsburg can be found in Misthallow. You should learn the history of the Rohirrim with Léothred.\n3\tTalk to Léothred at Framsburg\tFramsburg can be found in Misthallow. You should talk to Léothred at Framsburg.\n4\tDefeat giants in Misthallow (total: 2)\030Defeat trolls in Misthallow (total: 2)\030Defeat Wargs in Misthallow (total: 2)\tGiants may be found in Misthallow. You should seek out and defeat giants to learn more about Théodwyne Sternbrow.\n5\tReturn to Framsburg\tFramsburg can be found in Misthallow. You should return to Framsburg.\n6\tLearn the history of the Rohirrim with Léothred\tFramsburg can be found in Misthallow. You should learn the history of the Rohirrim with Léothred.\n7\tContinue learning the history of the Rohirrim with Léothred\tFramsburg can be found in Misthallow. You should learn the history of the Rohirrim with Léothred.\n8\tTalk to Léothred elsewhere at Framsburg\tFramsburg can be found in Misthallow. You should talk to Léothred at Framsburg.\n",
[6011]="70030745\n1\tDefeat half-orc bloodletters (total: 8)\030Defeat half-orc archers (total: 6)\tHalf-orcs can be found in the camps to the north-east of Garsfeld. You should thin out the encroaching forces in the hopes of encouraging the townsfolk of Garsfeld.\n2\tTalk to Gísil at the Mead Hall of Garsfeld\tGísil can be found in the Mead Hall of Garsfeld, south-west of the half-orc camp. You should bring news of your victories to Gísil.\n",
[6012]="70062DDD\n1\tDefeat half-orcs in Sedgemead or Ruddymore (total: 6)\tMelona told you that Bedwyr has worked in the past with half-orcs, and he might have gone looking for such allies at a bridge to the north.\n2\tRead the discarded parchment on the bridge defended by half-orcs\tThe bridge across the river in Sedgemead might hold some clue to Bedwyr's location.\n3\tTalk to Melona in Sedgemead\tMelona is waiting for you where you met her, south of the bridge defended by half-orcs in Sedgemead.\n",
[6013]="70037158\n1\tYou should dispatch some of the half-orc scouts threatening the farms and fields of the Broadacres.\t\n2\tDefeat half-orc warriors (total: 3)\030Defeat half-orc riders (total: 6)\tMounted half-orcs may be found throughout the fields south of Torsbury. You should dispatch some of the half-orc scouts threatening the farms and fields of the Broadacres.\n",
[6014]="70007041\n1\tReturn the relics to Hunulf Munce\030Collect relics (total: 10)\tThe ruins of Naerost are just east of Weathertop, north of Hunulf's camp. A year ago, half-orcs wrested the ruins of Naerost from the Eglain, causing the Eglain to lose a valuable source of trade-goods. Hunulf asked you to return to ruins to sift through the relics there to recover the trade-goods they lost.\n",
[6015]="70037154\n1\tDefeat Egur\tYou should hunt down and defeat the captain of the half-orc riders in the western part of the Broadacres.\n2\tDefeat Egur\tEgur may be found in the fields south of Torsbury. You should hunt down and defeat the captain of the half-orc riders in the western part of the Broadacres.\n3\tCompleted\tYou have defeated Egur, the captain of the half-orc riders in the western part of the Broadacres.\n",
[6016]="70002C93\n1\tSearch for the half-orc who planted the powder\tThe half-orc rumoured to have been in Trestlebridge can likely be found in the Orc camp north-east of Trestlebridge. You should search for anyone matching Aggy Digweed's description.\n2\tReturn to Aggy Digweed\tAggy Digweed is in Trestlebridge. You should return to Aggy Digweed with news of your victory against Lugbas.\n",
})
